cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "snakemake_debug: a low-alignment / contamination diagnostics Snakemake workflow"
abstract: >-
  A reusable, containerized Snakemake workflow that diagnoses why short-read
  samples align poorly to their reference: per-sample alignment rates, motif
  signatures of the unaligned reads, remote BLAST identification, contaminant-
  and custom-genome screens, Kraken2 taxonomic classification, auto-selection of
  the top non-host organism, and a spike-in multimapped-read investigation, with
  an interactive self-contained HTML report. Everything runs inside one Apptainer
  image.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ji"
    family-names: "Wang"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3443-5857"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_debug"
url: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_debug"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Snakemake
  - contamination diagnostics
  - unaligned reads
  - multimapping
  - spike-in sequencing
  - quality control
  - bioinformatics workflow
